      {
        "_uid": "b25c9143-57ae-6388-7cf1-160c95081c16",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Labelling head injuries amongst the commonest causes of death and disability in traffic related accidents in Pakistan, Dr Rehman explained that head injuries are no respectors of geography and occur on open highways and far-flung places, which make all the more difficult to provide timely medical attention by a qualified neurosurgeon. Dr Rehman highlighted that timely and efficient care in the initial few hours ofthe injury can significantly reduce the number of fatalities and disability associated with these serious injuries. He further stressed that dissemination of road traffic accidents, fights, falls and bullets which are responsible for death and disability in large number of patients.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A panel of Neurology and Neurosurgery Consultants also participated in the panel discussion, which included Dr Shahid Masud Baig and Dr Ahmed Ali Shah.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
