    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"In last 20 years, due to increased number of automobiles on the road, number of road traffic accidents have increased manifolds and will continue to multiply\", revealed Dr Naim-Ur- Rehman, Professor and Chief of Neurosurgery of the Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH). He was giving a presentation on \"Head Injuries\" at \"Signs, Symptoms and Care\", a monthly public health awareness program, held on May 29, 1999 at AKUH. Dr Rehman added that, \"infant two- third of the people who die as a result of traffic accidents, die from head injuries\".",
